# paper/ is GENERATED and byte-compared.
#
# tests/test_paper_artifacts.py rebuilds paper/ and compares NUMBERS.md, every
# table CSV and every figure-data CSV byte for byte. The builder always writes
# LF (newline="\n"). With core.autocrlf=true -- the default on Windows, and
# what this project is developed under -- git would hand a fresh clone CRLF
# working copies, and every one of those comparisons would fail for a reason
# that has nothing to do with a number moving.
#
# So: pin the generated text surface to LF in the working tree, and mark the
# rendered figures binary so git never touches them at all.
paper/**/*.csv   text eol=lf
paper/**/*.tex   text eol=lf
paper/**/*.txt   text eol=lf
paper/**/*.json  text eol=lf
paper/*.md       text eol=lf
paper/**/*.pdf   binary
paper/**/*.png   binary
